  "heading": "\\natural",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{natural}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\natural]\nDefines: n\nsatisfies:\n. oneOf:\n  . n = \\natural.0\n  . exists: m is \\natural\n    suchThat: n = \\natural.succ(m)\nRequires:\n. definition: \\natural.0 is \\natural\n. definition: \\natural.succ is (? is \\natural) -> (? is \\natural)\nEnables:\n. capability: x_++ :=> \\natural.succ(x_)\n. capability: x_ + y_ :=> x_ \\.natural.+./ y_\nDocumented:\n. called: \"natural\"\n. description: \"A natural number is either $0$ or the successor of a natural\n                number, and these two cases are exclusive. Every natural number\n                is reached from $0$ by finitely many successors, which is the\n                basis for defining operations on the naturals by recursion.\"\nId: \"d88e480c-de0e-4e48-92b0-54bd232a346e\"",
